<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
        iOS 14.5+ requires apps that use the local network (including mDNS
        / Bonjour discovery) to declare:

        - NSLocalNetworkUsageDescription: a user-facing string shown in the
          one-time permission prompt the OS displays before any local-network
          traffic is allowed.
        - NSBonjourServices: an explicit allowlist of mDNS service types
          this app may browse for and advertise. Without this entry, iOS
          silently drops the mDNS queries even if the permission was granted.

        Without both, two iPhones on the same Wi-Fi cannot find each other
        via libp2p's mDNS discovery — they would have to bounce through the
        relay server, defeating the "direct P2P when possible" design.

        Service name `_p2p._udp` is libp2p's canonical mDNS service type per
        https://github.com/libp2p/specs/blob/master/discovery/mdns.md
        (the `.local` suffix is the DNS domain part, not included in
        NSBonjourServices).

        dx (Dioxus CLI) 0.7+ merges this file with its generated Info.plist
        via the `ios_info_plist = "info.plist"` key in Dioxus.toml.
    -->
    <key>NSLocalNetworkUsageDescription</key>
    <string>WaveSyncDB syncs with nearby devices on your local network without going through a server, so changes you make on one device appear instantly on others on the same Wi-Fi.</string>

    <key>NSBonjourServices</key>
    <array>
        <string>_p2p._udp</string>
    </array>
</dict>
</plist>
